   "heading": "FINITE AND p -ADIC POLYLOGARITHMS 1. Introduction The ﬁnite logarithm was introduced by Kontsevich (under the name “The 1 1 logarithm”) in [Kon]. The ﬁnite logarithm is the case n = 1 of the n -th polylogarithm li n ∈ Z /p [ z ] deﬁned by li n ( z ) = P p − 1 k =1 z k /k n . In loc. cit. Kontsevich",
